    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0252" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1881: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-13T16:00:00-04:00">June 13, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>154. Department’s 138, May 22 [<hi rendition="#italic">27</hi>]. War Department
                    prefers not to undertake organization of mission to Iran at this time. Reasons
                    given are: 1. Difficulty of releasing experienced officers for such duty; 2.
                    Primary responsibility of British for Middle Eastern operations; 3. War
                    Department doubts that foreign mission could have much effect in correction
                    abuses in Iranian Army.</p>
                <p>However, it is understood General Greely will be instructed to make a report upon
                    all phases of situation, and if he recommends assignment of additional officers
                    further consideration will be given the proposal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
